{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: All four completed experiments use pca_n2000 for RNA and singleprofile. RNA is clearly the dominant modality (0.485 vs 0.208 image-only), and multimodal concat adds ~4 pts over RNA-only. However, PCA is a purely linear, untrained dimensionality reduction, and we have zero evidence about whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200, scgpt) could substantially improve the RNA representation. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether the RNA encoder choice is a high-leverage design decision or whether PCA already captures most of the useful signal. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_002 (same fusion, same image encoder, same profile setting; only RNA encoder changes from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200). If scvi_n200 substantially outperforms PCA, it tells us to invest in learned RNA representations going forward; if it performs similarly, PCA is sufficient and we should prioritize other axes (multiprofile, image encoder). Under a limited budget, isolating the RNA encoder effect on the dominant modality is the highest-information next step before committing to more complex multiprofile or fusion architectures."
}

